and  and at sea  the natural beauty of nova scotia is  undisturbed but the soul of this  province has been darkened  the anxiety felt by all canadians in  2020  can't compare to the blanket of grief  here an anguish that's stricken everyone  i've cried more  in the last 10 months than certainly i  did in the first seven years of my job  but really probably ever mourning dozens  of deaths from covet 19  and a string of other tragedies i think  we are requesting  more ambulances probably one more coming  and then at least one more standby only  a few weeks into the pandemic  came april's hideous massacre a  denturist  dressed up like a mountie killed 13  people in the tiny village of portopic  he killed nine more people in other  communities the next day  before being shot dead by police this  grief counselor says  devastation from the slaughter is  unshakable it's changed  um there's uh i mean i feel it when i'm  out on my walks  there's a beauty and a sadness all  intertwined now  before the end of april tragedy struck  again a navy helicopter based in halifax  crashed off the coast of greece all six  people on board were killed in the prime  of their lives  including navy sub-lieutenant abigail  cobra then there's the more personal  items you know walking her down the  aisle when she decides to get married  first child those types of things that  just  won't ever happen less than three weeks  after the helicopter went down  a canadian forces snowbirds jet crashed  after takeoff in kamloops bc  the crash killed captain jen casey a  nova scotia native  working as a public affairs officer 2020  is a year i'd like to forget and we're  not even halfway there yet  in september more distress this time in  the nova scotia lobster fishery  indigenous fishers exercising their  treaty rights  were confronted by commercial harvesters  [Applause]  commercial fishers sabotage fishing  lines a lobster pound that did business  with indigenous harvesters was burnt to  the ground  in a dispute that intensified for weeks  and is still  unresolved yet another painful episode  that made 2020  the most trying year in recent memory  i've never seen anything like it and and  you know i cried too i don't know  anybody who didn't cry  but sorrow can also inspire  dimitri nionakis used his piloting  skills to provide consolation  by recording intricate flight paths on  gps  neonak has created sky drawings like a  heart for port-a-pick  flying hundreds of kilometers for each  artistic tribute  he spelled out jen casey's name and he  traced an anchor in the sky for yet  another heartbreaking disaster  december's sinking of a scalloped dragon  near digby  which claimed the lives of six men  risking his own safety and poor flying  conditions  neonakus helped raise 60 thousand  dollars for the men's families  those messages from people who lost  their parents or lost their brother or  sister  messages they mean a lot to me those  those messages  those are the ones that they hit home  another positive  is the overall success of nova scotia  and the atlantic region  in limiting the spread of covet 19.  grief counselors  say moral victories don't erase the  impact of unimaginable tragedy  it's absolutely devastating they say  time  and space are critically important as  efforts to heal  continue into the new year ross lord  global news  halifax still ahead bidding farewell to  2020 how the world is starting a new  year  with new hope  new year's eve is often a time of  reflection and when we think of 2020  it is going to be remembered for  bringing us a pandemic unlike anything  we've experienced in our lifetimes  before  in one way or another it's had an impact  on us all  the world over for much of the globe the  year has already  ended redmond shannon takes a look at  how the planet  is ringing in 2021  normally sydney harbour is thronged with  thousands of people for new year's eve  but this year only those with restaurant  bookings were allowed up close  to see the iconic fireworks normally  there's crowds of people out and  it's a bit eerie this evening with new  virus clusters in the city  authorities asked aussies to watch from  home  although clearly not everyone listened  [Music]  the sensoji temple bell rang in 2021 in  tokyo  a year the city hopes to host a delayed  olympics  daily cases of covet 19 have topped 1  000 in japan's capital for the first  time  and the governor has warned of an  explosion of cases  [Music]  in north korea little is known about the  extent of the pandemic  the crowds were dense but absolutely  everyone wore their mask  above their nose was leaked  german chancellor angela merkel called  2020 the most difficult of her 15 years  in office  taking aim at what she called cruel and  dangerous covet 19 conspiracy theories  in france an 8 p.m curfew was in place  with  dj david guetta playing a fundraising  gig from the louvre  this woman said she instead would be in  bed by eight  but in true french style would eat well  first  in london the traditional party spot of  trafalgar square opposite canada house  is off limits  most of the uk is in hard lockdown  catherine ryan  youtube uk has an online party hosted by  canadian comedian catherine ryan  join me with a few of my friends  somewhat optimistically encouraging  young people to party at home but wait  there is hope  jump back to the very start of the day  [Applause]  auckland new zealand no masks no worries  effectively covet free a sign of what  next new year's eve could be like  for all of us redmond shannon global  news london  and that is global national for this  thursday night and for 2020  i'm sonia dion for our final goodbye  we're going to  go out in style  [Music]  these goats are milking the party for  all it's worth  bleating in the new year from their home  in tennessee  rumor has it they'll be dancing to billy  vanilli  tonight on behalf of dorner robin and  the entire global national team wishing  you a very safe  and happy new year i'll see you back  here tomorrow  don't note  [Music]
 

